<http://data.silknow.org/object/73c19c01-315a-3277-a835-7cc175610732>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "The earliest samplers were reference works for embroiderers. They showed 'samples' of patterns and stitches and recorded how to achieve particular effects.  In Europe in the 17th century samplers provided instruction and practice for girls learning needlework. By the 18th century samplers were used to show more than just needlework skills. This example from 1827 includes a mathematical table alongside its alphabets and moral verse."@en , "Sampler of embroidered wool with red silk in cross stitch with eyelets. At the top are four rows of alphabets and a row of figures. In the centre, the multiplication table is arranged in a framework of squares with the crowns of various ranks from King to Marquis arranged on either side. At the bottom is a verse entitled 'Virtue', a row of hearts and other devices and a signature."@en , "Sampler of embroidered wool with silk, embroidered by Sarah Grace, England, dated 1827."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/8df88d02-d5eb-316c-96fd-7bfba1fbeca0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "The earliest samplers were reference works for embroiderers. They showed 'samples' of patterns and stitches and recorded how to achieve particular effects.  In Europe in the 17th century samplers provided instruction and practice for girls learning needlework. By the 18th century samplers were used to show more than just needlework skills. This example from 1827 includes a mathematical table alongside its alphabets and moral verse."@en , "Sampler of embroidered wool with red silk in cross stitch with eyelets. At the top are four rows of alphabets and a row of figures. In the centre, the multiplication table is arranged in a framework of squares with the crowns of various ranks from King to Marquis arranged on either side. At the bottom is a verse entitled 'Virtue', a row of hearts and other devices and a signature."@en , "Sampler of embroidered wool with silk, embroidered by Sarah Grace, England, dated 1827."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/73c19c01-315a-3277-a835-7cc175610732/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/73c19c01-315a-3277-a835-7cc175610732/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/73c19c01-315a-3277-a835-7cc175610732/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/73c19c01-315a-3277-a835-7cc175610732/dimension/2> ;
